{"id":"nursing-home-related-parties","title":"Related companies that Bay Area nursing homes deal with","question":"Which related companies do Bay Area nursing homes name in their State filings, and how many homes does each one serve?","finding":"145 Bay Area nursing homes (10 in San Francisco) are on the State’s list of 925 homes whose 2020 reports included a related company’s profit-and-loss statement. They name 110 related companies; 20 serve five or more Bay Area homes. The most named is PACS (16 Bay Area homes, 45 statewide). 15 of the names match a nursing-home chain in the federal chain file; the largest federal fine total among them is PACS Group with $8.9 million across 275 homes nationwide.","how":"The State health-data department’s list of 2020 long-term care financial reports that included related-party statements, with county added from the State’s licensed-facility listing by the downloader (Bay Area here means the six counties so flagged in that file: Alameda, Contra Costa, Marin, San Francisco, San Mateo and Santa Clara). Related-company names are grouped when they are the same after removing punctuation and company suffixes. Chain figures are the 2026-09 edition of the federal chain file, matched when the related company’s name equals the chain’s name, or one begins with the other, after dropping general words such as Group, Services, Management and Holdings; fines and payment denials are national totals for the whole chain, as that file counts them. The last column is the same kind of name match to company owners in this project’s Medicare ownership screen, with the number of Medicare providers listed there under that owner.","limits":"Buying services, supplies or the use of a building from a company under the same ownership has to be disclosed. The State collects the related company’s profit-and-loss statement with the home’s yearly report and publishes which homes filed one; a State fact sheet adds that from fiscal years ending December 31, 2023 operators must also file combined accounts covering related companies that share 5% or more common ownership and serve the home. This list says who disclosed such dealings, not that anything was wrong. The list covers report periods ending in 2020 only, names the related companies without amounts, and does not say what each one supplied. A related company serving many homes is what a chain is. Chain matches are by name: a supplier and a chain can share a name without being the same business, and federal fines belong to the chain’s homes across the country, not to the Bay Area homes listed. Spellings are kept as filed, so one company may appear under two spellings.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"party","t":"Related company named","type":"org"},{"k":"bayArea","t":"Bay Area homes naming it","type":"int"},{"k":"sanFrancisco","t":"Of them in San Francisco","type":"int"},{"k":"california","t":"Homes statewide","type":"int"},{"k":"counties","t":"Bay Area counties","type":"text"},{"k":"sfHomes","t":"San Francisco homes","type":"text"},{"k":"chain","t":"Federal chain file: matching name","type":"text"},{"k":"chainHomes","t":"Chain’s homes nationwide","type":"int"},{"k":"chainFineCount","t":"Chain’s federal fines","type":"int"},{"k":"chainFines","t":"Chain’s fines, dollars","type":"usd"},{"k":"chainDenials","t":"Chain’s payment denials","type":"int"},{"k":"medicareOwner","t":"Medicare ownership screen: matching name","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"party":"PACS","partyKey":null,"bayArea":16,"sanFrancisco":3,"california":45,"counties":"Alameda 6, Contra Costa 5, San Francisco 3, Marin 1, San Mateo 1","sfHomes":"Central Gardens Post Acute; San Francisco Post Acute; Victorian Post Acute","chain":"PACS Group","chainHomes":275,"chainFines":8869359,"chainFineCount":256,"chainDenials":70,"medicareOwner":"Pacs Holdings, Llc (128 Medicare providers)"},{"party":"Life Generations Healthcare","partyKey":null,"bayArea":11,"sanFrancisco":2,"california":25,"counties":"Santa Clara 3, Contra Co